{"step_index":94,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:59:11Z","content":"Both **Set A** and **Set B** (Question Papers & Marking Schemes) have been updated in **MS Word (`.docx`)** format with embedded high-contrast diagrams and 100% rationalized NCERT syllabus compliance.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Embedded High-Contrast Diagrams\nClear, centrally-aligned figures have been embedded in the Word documents:\n\n* **Case Study 1 (Q36 — Relations & Functions):**\n  * **Set A:** Partition diagram of $A = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$ into Odd $[1]=\\{1,3,5\\}$ and Even $[2]=\\{2,4\\}$ equivalence classes.\n  * **Set B:** Directed relation graph showing divisibility on $A = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 6\\}$.\n* **Case Study 2 (Q37 — Application of Derivatives):**\n  * **Set A:** Production Total Cost Curve $C(x) = 0.005x^3 - 0.02x^2 + 30x + 5000$ indicating point $x = 3$.\n  * **Set B:** Total Revenue Curve $R(x) = 13x^2 + 26x + 15$ indicating marginal revenue point $x = 7$.\n* **Case Study 3 (Q38 — Integrals):**\n  * **Set A:** Velocity–Time curve $v(t) = 3t^2 - 12t + 9$ with shaded displacement area and rest points ($t = 1\\text{ s}, 3\\text{ s}$).\n  * **Set B:** Velocity–Time curve $v(t) = 6t^2 - 4t$ with displacement area and rest point ($t = 2/3\\text{ s}$).\n* **Assertion–Reason Questions (Q19 & Q20):**\n  * **Set A:** Graph of $y = |x - 2|$ (corner point at $x = 2$) and parabola $y = -(x - 3)^2 + 4$ (maximum at $(3, 4)$).\n  * **Set B:** Step graph of $y = [x]$ (step discontinuities at integers) and curve $y = \\ln x$ (monotonic increase).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Deleted Syllabus Audit & Corrections\nA thorough audit of the rationalized NCERT Class XII curriculum was conducted, and the following questions were corrected:\n\n* **Tangents & Normals (Chapter 6 — Deleted from Rationalized NCERT):**\n  * **Set A Q15 (MCQ):** Replaced with finding the maximum value of $f(x) = \\sin x + \\cos x$ on $[0, \\pi/2]$.\n  * **Set A Q16 (MCQ):** Replaced with computing Marginal Revenue for $R(x) = 3x^2 + 36x + 5$ at $x = 15$.\n  * **Set A Q24 (2M):** Replaced with rate of change of cube volume ($dV/dt$) given edge rate.\n  * **Set B Q15 (MCQ):** Replaced with rate of change of total surface area of a sphere ($dS/dr$).\n  * **Set B Q24 (2M):** Replaced with rate of change of circle area ($dA/dt$).\n* **Other Chapters:** Zero composite/invertible functions (Ch 1), zero inverse trig property proofs (Ch 2), zero elementary row operations (Ch 3), zero determinant property proofs (Ch 4), and zero Rolle's/MVT (Ch 5).\n\n---\n\n### 3. File Access Links\n\nDirectory: `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\`\n\n| Document | Word Document (`.docx`) | Text Source (`.txt`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Set A Question Paper** | [Set_A_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.docx) | [Set_A_Question_Paper.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.txt) |\n| **Set A Marking Scheme** | [Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx) | [Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt) |\n| **Set B Question Paper** | [Set_B_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.docx) | [Set_B_Question_Paper.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.txt) |\n| **Set B Marking Scheme** | [Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx) | [Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt) |"}
