{"step_index":96,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:02:11Z","thinking":"**Investigating Image Alignment**\n\nI'm now diving into image alignment issues within the `python-docx` environment. Specifically, I'm examining scenarios where images might be improperly displayed or not visible. I've started by focusing on how paragraph styles impact image rendering, hoping to pinpoint the root cause of these alignment problems.\n\n\n**Addressing Image Clipping**\n\nI've determined that fixed line spacing in paragraphs containing inline images is the culprit behind the clipping issue. Using fixed line spacing, such as 14pt, or inheriting from a style with a fixed height, leads to images being truncated. The solution involves ensuring the image paragraph uses either single line spacing or no line spacing constraint at all, alongside appropriate `space_before` and `space_after` settings.\n\n\n**Refining Image Dimensions**\n\nI've determined the ideal image width for documents is between 3.2 and 4.0 inches, aiming for roughly 7.26 inches. I'm also ensuring the images have bold lines, clear backgrounds, and high DPI for optimal rendering across themes. Reviewing the image generation code, I've noted the default line spacing in the `Normal` style is set to `Pt(14)`. This is problematic.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Enhanced diagram generator with crisp vector-like rasterization, solid white background, high contrast, and large fonts for perfect readability in MS Word.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nGenerate ultra-clear, high-contrast diagrams with solid white backgrounds\\nspecifically formatted for MS Word printing and digital viewing.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport os\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nIMG_DIR = r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\math_exam_2026\\\\images\\\"\\nos.makedirs(IMG_DIR, exist_ok=True)\\n\\n# Set styling\\nplt.rcParams['font.family'] = 'DejaVu Sans'\\nplt.rcParams['font.size'] = 11\\nplt.rcParams['font.weight'] = 'bold'\\nplt.rcParams['axes.edgecolor'] = '#000000'\\nplt.rcParams['axes.linewidth'] = 1.5\\n\\n\\ndef save_fig(fig, filename):\\n    filepath = os.path.join(IMG_DIR, filename)\\n    fig.patch.set_facecolor('white')\\n    plt.tight_layout()\\n    plt.savefig(filepath, dpi=300, facecolor='white', edgecolor='none', bbox_inches='tight')\\n    plt.close(fig)\\n    print(f\\\"Saved: {filename}\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ---------------- SET A DIAGRAMS ----------------\\n\\ndef gen_set_a_q19():\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Graph of f(x) = |x - 2|\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.8, 3.2))\\n    ax.set_facecolor('#FFFFFF')\\n    x = np.linspace(-1, 5, 400)\\n    y = np.abs(x - 2)\\n    ax.plot(x, y, color='#002B66', lw=3.0, label=r'$f(x) = |x - 2|$')\\n    ax.plot(2, 0, 'ro', markersize=8)\\n    ax.annotate('Corner at (2, 0)\\\\nContinuous but\\\\nNOT differentiable', xy=(2, 0), xytext=(2.2, 1.2),\\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1.5, headwidth=6),\\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=9.5, bbox=dict(boxstyle=\\\"square,pad=0.3\\\", fc=\\\"#FFF9E6\\\", ec=\\\"#CC9900\\\", lw=1.2))\\n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1.5)\\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1.5)\\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', color='#CCCCCC', alpha=0.8)\\n    ax.set_xlabel('x', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\\n    ax.set_ylabel('y', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\\n    ax.set_title('Figure 19: Continuity vs Differentiability of |x - 2|', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\\n    ax.set_ylim(-0.5, 3.5)\\n    ax.legend(loc='upper left', framealpha=0.95, facecolor='white', edgecolor='black')\\n    save\n<truncated 12547 bytes>","Description":"\"Updated high-contrast diagram generator with solid white background.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\b78a5d36-6586-4c94-a487-70da0c9f5362\\\\scratch\\\\generate_diagrams.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing diagram generator\"","toolSummary":"\"Update diagram generator\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
