{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:03:01Z","content":"The image alignment and visibility issue in MS Word has been resolved.\n\n### What Was Fixed\n\n1. **Paragraph Line Spacing (Fixed Clipping):** \n   - When paragraphs in MS Word have an exact line spacing (e.g. 14 pt), inline pictures get clipped to 14 pt height (appearing as thin/invisible strips). \n   - All image-containing paragraphs now explicitly use **Single Line Spacing** (`line_spacing_rule = SINGLE`) with **Center Alignment** (`alignment = CENTER`) and proper top/bottom spacing.\n2. **Solid White Backgrounds & High Contrast:**\n   - All figures have been re-rendered with solid opaque white backgrounds (`#FFFFFF`), thick 2.5–3.0 pt curves, and highlighted callout annotation boxes.\n3. **High Resolution & Optimal Sizing:**\n   - Rendered at **300 DPI** and sized at 3.5 to 4.0 inches wide, centered within standard A4 portrait narrow margins.\n\n---\n\n### Access the Updated Word Documents\n\nDirectory: `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\`\n\n* **Set A Question Paper:** [Set_A_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.docx)\n* **Set A Marking Scheme:** [Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx)\n* **Set B Question Paper:** [Set_B_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.docx)\n* **Set B Marking Scheme:** [Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx)"}
