{"step_index":108,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:08:08Z","thinking":"**Clarifying Matrix Notation**\n\nI'm now focusing on the specific formatting the user desires, especially regarding matrix and determinant notation within a Word document. I need to ensure I can accurately render these mathematical expressions using the appropriate bracket symbols for 3x3 matrices and others. I'm exploring the conventions used in Word's formula editor.\n\n\n**Investigating OMML Implementation**\n\nI'm now deep-diving into OMML (Office Math Markup Language) to understand how Word natively formats matrices. Specifically, I'm examining the `<m:oMath>`, `<m:d>`, and `<m:m>` tags, and the implications of square brackets (`<m:begChr m:val=\"[\"/>`, `<m:endChr m:val=\"]\"/>`) for matrix notation. It appears `python-docx` is able to insert these native equations through OMML! I'm verifying the XML namespace: `xmlns:m=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\"` as the key to unlocking this.\n\n\n**Decoding OMML Structures**\n\nI'm now closely examining the OMML code for both matrix and determinant representations. I'm focusing on how the `<m:m>` (matrix) and `<m:d>` (delimiter) elements are structured and combined. Specifically, how `<m:begChr>` and `<m:endChr>` define the delimiters, either brackets or vertical bars, and how matrix entries are nested within `<m:mr>` (matrix row) and `<m:e>` (element). I can see that the `<m:plcHide m:val=\"on\"/>` tag hides placeholder characters.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Test script for inserting native MS Word OMML equation matrices and determinants.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nTest inserting native Word OMML equation matrices and determinants.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom docx import Document\\nfrom docx.oxml import parse_xml\\nfrom docx.oxml.ns import nsdecls\\n\\ndef create_omml_matrix(rows, bracket='['):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rows: list of lists of strings, e.g. [['1', '2'], ['3', '4']]\\n    bracket: '[' for matrix, '|' for determinant, '(' for paren matrix\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if bracket == '[':\\n        beg_chr, end_chr = '[', ']'\\n    elif bracket == '|':\\n        beg_chr, end_chr = '|', '|'\\n    elif bracket == '(':\\n        beg_chr, end_chr = '(', ')'\\n    else:\\n        beg_chr, end_chr = '[', ']'\\n        \\n    mr_xml_list = []\\n    for row in rows:\\n        e_xml_list = []\\n        for cell in row:\\n            e_xml_list.append(f'<m:e><m:r><m:t>{cell}</m:t></m:r></m:e>')\\n        mr_xml_list.append(f'<m:mr>{\\\"\\\".join(e_xml_list)}</m:mr>')\\n        \\n    m_body = \\\"\\\".join(mr_xml_list)\\n    \\n    xml = f\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    <m:oMath xmlns:m=\\\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\\\">\\n      <m:d>\\n        <m:dPr>\\n          <m:begChr m:val=\\\"{beg_chr}\\\"/>\\n          <m:endChr m:val=\\\"{end_chr}\\\"/>\\n          <m:grow m:val=\\\"on\\\"/>\\n        </m:dPr>\\n        <m:e>\\n          <m:m>\\n            <m:mPr>\\n              <m:baseJc m:val=\\\"center\\\"/>\\n              <m:plcHide m:val=\\\"on\\\"/>\\n            </m:mPr>\\n            {m_body}\\n          </m:m>\\n        </m:e>\\n      </m:d>\\n    </m:oMath>\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return parse_xml(xml)\\n\\ndoc = Document()\\np = doc.add_paragraph(\\\"Let A = \\\")\\nomml = create_omml_matrix([['0', '1', '-2'], ['-1', '0', 'x'], ['2', '-3', '0']], bracket='[')\\np._element.append(omml)\\np.add_run(\\\" be a skew-symmetric matrix.\\\")\\n\\np2 = doc.add_paragraph(\\\"Evaluate the determinant: \\\")\\nomml_det = create_omml_matrix([['1', '2', '3'], ['0', '1', '4'], ['5', '6', '0']], bracket='|')\\np2._element.append(omml_det)\\n\\ndoc.save(r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\test_matrix.docx\\\")\\nprint(\\\"Saved test_matrix.docx successfully!\\\")\\n\"","Description":"\"Test script for OMML matrix and determinant generator.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\b78a5d36-6586-4c94-a487-70da0c9f5362\\\\scratch\\\\test_matrix.py\"","toolAction":"\"Testing OMML matrices\"","toolSummary":"\"Test OMML generation\""}}]}
