{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:08:37Z","thinking":"**Developing Exam Materials**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing `generate_all_exam_materials.py`. It leverages `make_omml_matrix` to ensure comprehensive coverage. I'm aiming to include all matrices (2x2, 3x3) and determinants (3x3) across question papers and marking schemes. I'm meticulously checking every instance to guarantee uniformity and correctness in the application.\n\n\n**Analyzing Determinants' Occurrences**\n\nI've pinpointed multiple determinant instances within the Set A question paper. Specifically, questions 6, 28, and several others feature 2x2 and 3x3 matrices and determinants, including evaluating them and finding values. I'm noting the context to see if there are common methods across all these instances.\n\n\n**Examining Linear Equations**\n\nI'm now diving into Set B's question paper. I see questions involving determinants (Q6, Q28), matrix operations (Q22), and matrix decomposition (Q32). I'm looking at how these concepts are tested and applied, with a keen eye on identifying underlying patterns. Question 33, involving a matrix method, requires further analysis of how this is applied.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Complete script generating Set A & Set B Question Papers and Marking Schemes with native MS Word OMML brackets for 3x3, 2x2 matrices and determinants.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nGenerate complete Set A and Set B Question Papers and Marking Schemes\\nwith:\\n1. Native MS Word OMML equation brackets for all matrices (3x3, 2x2, 3x1 vectors) and determinants.\\n2. Centered, high-contrast 300 DPI diagrams with solid white backgrounds and no clipping.\\n3. 100% NCERT rationalized syllabus compliance.\\n4. Strict Times New Roman 12pt, A4 portrait, narrow margin formatting with no box separators.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport os\\nfrom docx import Document\\nfrom docx.shared import Pt, Cm, Inches, RGBColor\\nfrom docx.enum.text import WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH, WD_LINE_SPACING\\nfrom docx.enum.section import WD_ORIENT\\nfrom docx.oxml import parse_xml\\n\\nOUT_DIR = r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\math_exam_2026\\\"\\nIMG_DIR = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"images\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef make_omml_matrix(rows, bracket='['):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rows: 2D list of strings, e.g. [['1', '2'], ['3', '4']]\\n    bracket: '[' for square bracket matrix, '|' for determinant, '(' for paren\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    beg_chr = '|' if bracket == '|' else ('(' if bracket == '(' else '[')\\n    end_chr = '|' if bracket == '|' else (')' if bracket == '(' else ']')\\n    \\n    mr_xml_list = []\\n    for row in rows:\\n        e_xml_list = []\\n        for cell in row:\\n            e_xml_list.append(f'<m:e><m:r><m:rPr><m:scr m:val=\\\"roman\\\"/><m:sty m:val=\\\"p\\\"/></m:rPr><m:t>{cell}</m:t></m:r></m:e>')\\n        mr_xml_list.append(f'<m:mr>{\\\"\\\".join(e_xml_list)}</m:mr>')\\n        \\n    m_body = \\\"\\\".join(mr_xml_list)\\n    \\n    xml = f\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    <m:oMath xmlns:m=\\\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\\\">\\n      <m:d>\\n        <m:dPr>\\n          <m:begChr m:val=\\\"{beg_chr}\\\"/>\\n          <m:endChr m:val=\\\"{end_chr}\\\"/>\\n          <m:grow m:val=\\\"on\\\"/>\\n        </m:dPr>\\n        <m:e>\\n          <m:m>\\n            <m:mPr>\\n              <m:baseJc m:val=\\\"center\\\"/>\\n              <m:plcHide m:val=\\\"on\\\"/>\\n            </m:mPr>\\n            {m_body}\\n          </m:m>\\n        </m:e>\\n      </m:d>\\n    </m:oMath>\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return pa\n<truncated 52332 bytes>","Description":"\"Master generator for Question Papers and Marking Schemes with OMML bracket matrices and determinants.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\