{"step_index":125,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:13:57Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Matrix Display**\n\nI've zeroed in on the user's observation about the incomplete matrix display – specifically, why only a single row is visible instead of the full 3x3. I think I have a hypothesis on this. It seems like a potential display issue within the software, like a default setting, rather than a deeper problem.\n\n\n**Investigating Vertical Clipping**\n\nI believe I've pinpointed a key cause: vertical clipping within MS Word when dealing with inline math objects like the user's matrix. Specifically, fixed line spacing like 14pt can cause tall inline equations (e.g., a 3x3 matrix) to be cut off vertically, leaving only one row visible. The line box prevents viewing the full matrix. This suggests that the solution is to remove fixed line spacing or use single/automatic line spacing so Word adjusts to fit the full object.\n\n\n**Confirming Clipping Cause**\n\nI've been reviewing the code and can now definitively confirm the root of the clipping issue. The `line_spacing = Pt(14)` setting was applied consistently to all paragraphs containing matrices, including in Questions 6, 22, 28, and 32, and in the marking schemes. This fixed line spacing caused Word to restrict the line height, thus truncating the matrix display, making only one row visible. I plan to test this hypothesis shortly.\n\n\n**Refining Spacing Solution**\n\nI've been improving the spacing fix further. Now, rather than manually adjusting line spacing for each matrix, I'm integrating automatic line spacing into the document creation process. I'm testing a new `add_math_p` function that consistently uses single line spacing for math paragraphs. Additionally, I'm updating `create_base_doc()` to set the \"Normal\" style to use a relative (e.g., 1.15 multiple) or single line spacing, instead of the fixed 14pt. I'm confident this will prevent future matrix display truncations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Python script to test matrix line height expansion with relative line spacing in MS Word.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nTest script to verify all 9 elements of a 3x3 matrix are visible in Word.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom docx import Document\\nfrom docx.shared import Pt, Inches\\nfrom docx.enum.text import WD_LINE_SPACING, WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH\\nfrom docx.oxml import parse_xml\\n\\ndef make_omml_matrix(rows, bracket='['):\\n    beg_chr = '|' if bracket == '|' else '['\\n    end_chr = '|' if bracket == '|' else ']'\\n    mr_xml_list = []\\n    for row in rows:\\n        e_xml_list = []\\n        for cell in row:\\n            e_xml_list.append(f'<m:e><m:r><m:rPr><m:scr m:val=\\\"roman\\\"/><m:sty m:val=\\\"p\\\"/></m:rPr><m:t>{cell}</m:t></m:r></m:e>')\\n        mr_xml_list.append(f'<m:mr>{\\\"\\\".join(e_xml_list)}</m:mr>')\\n        \\n    m_body = \\\"\\\".join(mr_xml_list)\\n    xml = f\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    <m:oMath xmlns:m=\\\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\\\">\\n      <m:d>\\n        <m:dPr>\\n          <m:begChr m:val=\\\"{beg_chr}\\\"/>\\n          <m:endChr m:val=\\\"{end_chr}\\\"/>\\n          <m:grow m:val=\\\"on\\\"/>\\n        </m:dPr>\\n        <m:e>\\n          <m:m>\\n            <m:mPr>\\n              <m:baseJc m:val=\\\"center\\\"/>\\n              <m:plcHide m:val=\\\"on\\\"/>\\n            </m:mPr>\\n            {m_body}\\n          </m:m>\\n        </m:e>\\n      </m:d>\\n    </m:oMath>\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return parse_xml(xml)\\n\\ndoc = Document()\\n# Set Normal style with SINGLE spacing (not Pt(14) fixed)\\nstyle = doc.styles['Normal']\\npf = style.paragraph_format\\npf.space_before = Pt(0)\\npf.space_after = Pt(2)\\npf.line_spacing_rule = WD_LINE_SPACING.SINGLE\\npf.line_spacing = None\\n\\np = doc.add_paragraph()\\np.paragraph_format.line_spacing_rule = WD_LINE_SPACING.SINGLE\\np.paragraph_format.line_spacing = None\\np.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(4)\\nr = p.add_run(\\\"6. The value of x for which the matrix A = \\\")\\np._element.append(make_omml_matrix([['0', '1', '-2'], ['-1', '0', 'x'], ['2', '-3', '0']], bracket='['))\\np.add_run(\\\" is skew-symmetric, is:\\\\n(a) 3   (b) -3   (c) 2   (d) -2\\\")\\n\\np2 = doc.add_paragraph()\\np2.paragraph_format.line_spacing_rule = WD_LINE_SPACING\n<truncated 429 bytes>","Description":"\"Test script for matrix display with single line spacing.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\b78a5d36-6586-4c94-a487-70da0c9f5362\\\\scratch\\\\test_matrix_fixed.py\"","toolAction":"\"Testing matrix height fix\"","toolSummary":"\"Test matrix height fix\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
