{"step_index":135,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:15:45Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Updated walkthrough explaining the fix for full 3x3 matrix height expansion (showing all 9 elements and full brackets) by setting dynamic Single Line Spacing.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Half-Yearly Examination 2026–27: Class XII Mathematics\\n## Final Walkthrough & Updated Delivery\\n\\n### Summary of Completed Files\\nAll Question Papers and Marking Schemes have been updated with:\\n1. **Dynamic Line Height for Matrices & Determinants:**\\n   - Paragraphs containing $3 \\\\times 3$ matrices, $2 \\\\times 2$ matrices, and $3 \\\\times 3$ determinants now explicitly use **Single Line Spacing (`line_spacing_rule = SINGLE`, `line_spacing = None`)**.\\n   - This allows Microsoft Word to **dynamically expand the line height** to fit all 3 rows (all 9 elements) and brackets, resolving the vertical clipping issue where only 1 row (3 numbers) was visible.\\n2. **Native MS Word OMML Equation Brackets:**\\n   - **Square Brackets $[ \\\\dots ]$** for all $3 \\\\times 3$, $2 \\\\times 2$ matrices and column vectors ($X, B$).\\n   - **Vertical Bar Brackets $| \\\\dots |$** for all $3 \\\\times 3$ determinants.\\n3. **High-Contrast 300 DPI Embedded Diagrams:**\\n   - Solid white backgrounds for Case Studies and Assertion–Reason questions without picture clipping.\\n4. **100% NCERT Rationalized Syllabus Compliance:**\\n   - Zero deleted syllabus topics (Tangents & Normals replaced with Rate of Change, Maxima/Minima, Revenue/Cost).\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### File Locations\\nDirectory: `C:\\\\Users\\\\rajan\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\math_exam_2026\\\\`\\n\\n1. **Set A Question Paper**\\n   - Word Document: [Set_A_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.docx)\\n   - Text Source: